<output_format>
Generate a Markdown document.
Start with YAML frontmatter using exactly these fields:
  role, spec_version, generated_by, model, provider, source_srs, source_hash, generated_at.
Include these sections:
  - Test Strategy (testing pyramid: unit/integration/E2E split, tooling choices)
  - Test Environment Setup (how to bootstrap test data, seed scripts, env variables)
  - Unit Test Cases (table: test ID, module, scenario, expected outcome)
  - Integration Test Cases (API contract tests, service-to-service tests)
  - End-to-End Test Cases (user flow scenarios matching personas from 01_product_manager.md)
  - Edge Cases and Negative Tests (boundary conditions, invalid inputs, race conditions)
  - Coverage Requirements (minimum % per layer, what is excluded and why)
  - CI Integration (when tests run, parallelization, flakiness policy)
  - Performance Tests (load test scenarios, acceptance thresholds)
  - Security Tests (auth bypass attempts, injection, OWASP checklist)
  - Open Questions (unresolved QA decisions)
</output_format>

<constraints>
- Be specific to THIS project, not generic. Reference concrete details from the SRS.
- Every E2E test case must map to a named persona from 01_product_manager.md.
- Every API endpoint from 02_backend_lead.md must have at least one happy-path and one error-path test case.
- Coverage thresholds must be specific numbers (e.g., "80% line coverage on services/").
- CI section must specify: which pipeline stages run which suites, and what constitutes a blocking failure.
- Edge cases must include: concurrent requests, empty states, pagination boundaries, auth token expiry.
- Performance thresholds must be measurable: "p95 response time < 300ms under 100 concurrent users".
- Do not list tests as "TBD" — write actual scenario descriptions.
</constraints>

